; the settings and key in ENVARC:Claude are yours and stay
; C:ClaudeCode: the second program of Claude.lha 1.0, one app since CL1; an old copy goes too
Delete >NIL: C:Claude C:ClaudeCode QUIET
; C:uptelnet is UP-Term.lha's program too: it stays while UP-Term is installed (its Uninstall
; removes it when no Claude record is left)
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If WARN
  Delete >NIL: C:uptelnet QUIET
EndIf
; the quick-launch icons in UP-Term: (only when there is an UP-Term: to look in)
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If NOT WARN
  Delete >NIL: UP-Term:Claude UP-Term:Claude.info UP-Term:ClaudeCode UP-Term:ClaudeCode.info QUIET
EndIf
